  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile with scvi_n200 yields the best results (0.650-0.653), a large jump over singleprofile scvi (0.520) and singleprofile pca (0.485). Aggregation (avgpool vs transformer) is negligible (~0.3%). Uncertainty: We do not know whether the multiprofile gain is a general property of multi-view profiling or is specifically enabled by the learned scvi representation. This experiment (pca_n2000 + multiprofile + avgpool) directly isolates the encoder effect in the multiprofile regime by holding profile setting and aggregation fixed while swapping scvi→pca. If pca+multiprofile approaches 0.65, the encoder is secondary and simpler pipelines suffice; if it drops substantially, learned encoders are essential for multiprofile to work. This is the highest-information single comparison available: it clarifies the encoder×profile interaction in the performance-critical regime before investing budget in multimodal or scgpt variants that build on an untested assumption about which encoder to use."
}

